    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** centers on an elite opportunity for **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.14), who provides our highest ceiling against the right-handed Law. **Vinnie Pasquantino** thrives with a significant +14% dynamic platoon boost, effectively weaponizing his contact profile in this matchup. Joining him as a priority start is **Trevor Story** (67.25), whose combination of a favorable park and a soft SP_xERA of 4.48 makes him a cornerstone play. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** (63.28) is a lock; while his base projection is solid, the combination of batting second and an 85% stolen base opportunity against Gasser makes him a high-leverage asset in our pursuit of scarcity points. **Griffin Conine** (60.12) also sneaks into our strong-start tier, capitalizing on a weak 5.63 SP_xERA matchup to justify his promotion to the active roster.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Zach McKinstry**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 39.94 score, falling just shy of our 40-point threshold. While his park factors were positive, the combination of a tough SP_xERA (3.41) and a negative platoon shift rendered him a net-negative compared to our utility options. Elsewhere, **Max Muncy** (44.47) and **Austin Riley** (41.94) present significant risks today. Both are facing elite arms (Cease and Luzardo, respectively), and while their park factors keep them above our bench floor, their sub-45 scores make them the most vulnerable spots in the lineup. We are monitoring **Corbin Carroll**, who remains on the bench due to his absence from the official starting lineup; should he be inserted as a late defensive replacement or pinch-hitter, his elite sprint speed would be a massive boon, but we cannot rely on his output at this time.\n\nLooking across the rest of the bench, **Josh Naylor** and **Tyler Soderstrom** are unavailable due to schedule and injury constraints, respectively, leaving **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** in reserve. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Gabriel Moreno** (56.71) and **James Wood** (50.12); both are facing tough opposition and must rely on their high-order placement\u2014#3 and #1, respectively\u2014to sustain their daily efficiency. We will continue to prioritize stolen base potential throughout the afternoon to ensure **Ghost Ride the WHIP** maintains its edge in a tightly contested 5x5 landscape.",
